+# R1 capability and API inventory
+
+**Inventory baseline:** `refactor/modern-cpp@32800f03a5d47f997b1a0c70460bad83fcf7faf7`
+
+This inventory distinguishes code that exists from behavior that R1 is willing to
+call supported. It is the evidence/status input for issues #41–#52 and should be
+updated when later work changes a status.
+
+## Status definitions
+
+| Status | Meaning in R1 |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Supported** | Intended public R1 surface with direct regression/unit/oracle evidence for the stated scope. Known limits are listed explicitly. |
+| **Experimental** | Compiled or implemented code exists, but verification or integration is insufficient for a stable supported contract. Direct inclusion may be possible, but no stability promise is made. |
+| **Unimplemented** | Declaration/scaffolding exists without a usable formulation. It must not be advertised as functionality. |
+| **Internal** | Repository/build/binding/helper implementation, not part of the installed C++ API. |
+
+“Supported” is scoped. For example a section can be supported for area/inertia
+while a shear-center property is explicitly unavailable.
+
+## Production header inventory
+
+Every non-Eigen production header on the modern baseline has a destination and a
+public/internal decision below.
+
+| Current header | Types / functions | R1 status | Public? | First R1 destination | Evidence and limits |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `headers/particle.h` | `Dof`, `DOF`, `Mass`, `Particle` | Supported | Yes | `include/openvfife/core/particle.hpp` | `tests/test_particle.cpp`; exercised by all frame, oracle, and shim tests. Six storage slots are not six mandatory active DOFs. Translation mass-matrix time integration is explicitly rejected; invertible rotational inertia is supported. |
+| `headers/material.h` | `UniaxialMaterialState`, `BaseMaterial`, `LinearElastic`, `UniaxialPlastic`, `UniIdeal`, `UniBilinear`, `UniPower` | Mixed; see type table | Yes, except unsupported behavior is documented | `include/openvfife/material/material.hpp` | `tests/test_material.cpp`; `UniPower` has a known constitutive TODO and is not promoted as supported. The common contract is uniaxial, not a generic continuum law. |
+| `headers/section.h` | `BaseSection`, `CustomSectionParas`, `CustomSection`, `Ctube`, `AngleSteel`, `Rectangle` | Mixed; see type table | Yes | `include/openvfife/section/section.hpp` | Beam/oracle tests rely heavily on `CustomSection`; section-specific evidence varies. Calculated shear center is unavailable for `Ctube`, `AngleSteel`, and `Rectangle` and currently becomes zero after a diagnostic. |
+| `headers/integrator.h` | `BaseIntegrator`, `GaussLegendre`, `GaussLobatto` | Supported spatial quadrature | Yes | `include/openvfife/numerics/quadrature.hpp` | `tests/test_integrator.cpp` covers constant 1D/2D/3D integration, order bounds, invalid inputs, and index errors. This is spatial quadrature, not time stepping. |
+| `headers/gridsection.h` | `SectionPoint`, `CellNodes`, `SectionGridParameter`, `SectionCell`, `SectionResponse`, `SectionGrid`, `RectangleGrid`, `AngleSteelGrid`, `CreateGrid` | Experimental | Yes, experimental direct include; omit from initial umbrella | `include/openvfife/section/grid_section.hpp` | `tests/test_gridsection.cpp` unit-tests cells, response, damage, rectangle grids, factory errors, and deferred material assignment. No current production element consumes this subsystem after the plastic-beam classes were removed; valid `AngleSteelGrid` behavior is not directly regression-tested. |
+| `headers/element.h` | `Strain`, `Stress`, `ElementForce`, `BaseElement`, `StructElement`, `PlaneElement`, `SolidElement`, `Link2D`, `Link2DLD`, `Link3D`, `Link3DLD`, `Beam2D`, `Beam3D` | Mixed; see type table | Supported/experimental types public; stubs not documented as usable | `include/openvfife/element/element.hpp` | Direct element invariants, closed-form beams, frozen oracle, and shim regressions exist for only a subset. Common-base section/topology contracts are fixed in #43. |
+| `headers/structsystem.h` | `StructSystem`; `isFileExists`, `isDirExists`, `makedir` | `StructSystem`: Supported; file helpers: Internal | `StructSystem`: Yes; helpers: No | `include/openvfife/solver/struct_system.hpp`; file helpers move behind `src/io/` implementation | `tests/test_structsystem.cpp`, frame tests, frozen oracle, shim tests. #44 still has to enforce same-system membership/checked removal. Filesystem helpers are implementation detail, not library API. |
+| `headers/config.hpp` | `Config` and stream/template helpers | Internal legacy | No | `src/io/config.hpp` + implementation after #46 | No current production/test caller. Ordinary non-inline definitions in the header create a multi-TU ODR hazard. #46 decides whether to retain the utility internally or replace it; it is not installed as-is. |
+
+The bundled `headers/Eigen/` tree is third-party Eigen 3.4.0, not openVFIFE API.
+#47 owns its relocatable export/install treatment.
+
+## Type-level capability inventory
+
+### Core
+
+| Type/capability | Status | Evidence / boundary |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `Dof`, `DOF` | Supported | Typed DOF activation and constraint use are covered by `test_particle`, `test_structsystem`, beams and shim tests. |
+| `Mass` lumped mass | Supported | Positive/non-negative invariants and solver use covered by `test_particle` and element/system regressions. |
+| `Mass::rotation_mass_matrix` | Supported with constraint | `Particle` accepts it only when invertible for the active rotational solve; frozen integration probes exercise rotational inertia. |
+| `Mass::translate_mass_matrix` solve path | **Not supported** | `Particle::solve*` throws `logic_error`; `test_particle` requires rejection. Storage/setters existing does not make time integration available. |
+| `Particle` | Supported | Direct state/invariant tests plus all solver families. |
+
+### Materials
+
+| Type | Status | Evidence / limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `UniaxialMaterialState` | Supported | Explicit value-state contract used by link/section response; direct material and grid-section tests. History belongs to the response point/element, not the shared parameter object. |
+| `BaseMaterial` | Supported uniaxial extension contract | Current virtual response is scalar `update(delta_strain, state)`. It must not be described as a plane-stress/3D constitutive interface. |
+| `LinearElastic` | Supported | Direct update/state tests; beam/frame/oracle/shim paths. |
+| `UniaxialPlastic` | Supported as abstract uniaxial base | Used by concrete plastic material classes; not itself constructible. |
+| `UniBilinear` | Supported for tested uniaxial response | `test_material` covers elastic step, plastic return, unload state and parameter validation; WASM exposes it. |
+| `UniIdeal` | Experimental | Constructor/invariant rejection is tested, but no constitutive history regression establishes its numerical response. |
+| `UniPower` | Experimental / known numerical gap | Constructor invariants are tested, but `headers/material.h` still records that the constitutive update is not correct because last yield strain is not retained. R1 must not present it as verified. Repair is outside R1 completion. |
+
+### Sections
+
+| Type | Status | Evidence / limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `BaseSection` | Supported base for current structural elements | Public geometric property interface used throughout beam/link code. Some properties can be unavailable for specific derived shapes. |
+| `CustomSectionParas`, `CustomSection` | Supported | Primary section in Beam2D/Beam3D, frozen oracle, progression probes, shim, and direct section tests. `J <= 0` uses the documented polar fallback. |
+| `Rectangle` | Supported for geometry/grid usage | Used by `test_gridsection`; area/inertia formulation is production code. Calculated shear center is not implemented and must not be interpreted as verified zero. |
+| `AngleSteel` | Experimental/partial | Basic construction/area and invalid thickness are tested; `AngleSteelGrid` wrong-type rejection is tested. `calcSHy/calcSHz` are explicitly not defined and return zero after a diagnostic. No full section-property oracle exists. |
+| `Ctube` | Experimental | Implementation exists but no direct regression test covers it; calculated shear center is explicitly not defined. |
+
+### Spatial quadrature and section integration
+
+| Type | Status | Evidence / limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `BaseIntegrator` | Supported spatial quadrature base | Direct constant-integral and error tests. |
+| `GaussLegendre` | Supported for implemented orders 1–10 | Bounds/rejection and representative integration covered by `test_integrator`. |
+| `GaussLobatto` | Supported for implemented orders 2–10 | Bounds/rejection covered by `test_integrator`; used historically for section integration. |
+| `SectionPoint`, `CellNodes`, `SectionGridParameter` | Experimental data contracts | Unit-tested only through the experimental grid-section subsystem. |
+| `SectionCell`, `SectionResponse` | Experimental | Unit tests cover elastic response, damage, material assignment, and result aggregation, but no current supported element consumes them. |
+| `SectionGrid` | Experimental extension base | No supported production element currently depends on it. |
+| `RectangleGrid` | Experimental with unit evidence | Valid rectangle grid and invalid dimensions/cell count tested. |
+| `AngleSteelGrid` | Experimental with insufficient positive-path evidence | Type/error paths exist; no direct valid-grid numerical regression. |
+| `CreateGrid` | Experimental | Factory supports Rectangle/AngleSteel; unsupported section rejection tested. |
+
+### Elements
+
+| Type | Status | Evidence / limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `Strain`, `Stress`, `ElementForce` | Supported for current frame/link result contracts | Used by current elements/tests. They are not declared universal continuum result records. |
+| `BaseElement` | Supported common lifecycle/observer base with contract change pending | `test_element` checks particle-ID/length invariants through structural elements. #43 must make optional section and ordered topology explicit before continuum promotion. |
+| `StructElement` | Supported structural-family base | Required particle/material/section observers underpin all current beam/link formulations. |
+| `PlaneElement` | **Unimplemented** on modern baseline | Abstract TODO scaffolding; no production plane formulation on `refactor/modern-cpp`. Its current constructor/topology assumptions are not a stable extension contract. |
+| `SolidElement` | **Unimplemented** on modern baseline | Abstract TODO scaffolding; no production solid formulation on `refactor/modern-cpp`. |
+| `Link2D` | Supported | `test_beam2d` documented two-bar truss, element construction/invariant tests. |
+| `Link2DLD` | Experimental | Implementation exists and uses typed material state, but current native regression suite has no direct numerical case for this class. |
+| `Link3D` | Experimental | Constructibility is checked; no direct force/displacement numerical regression in the modern suite. |
+| `Link3DLD` | Experimental | Implementation and WASM exposure exist, but current native tests do not exercise a numerical `kind=3` model. |
+| `Beam2D` | Supported | Closed-form axial, cantilever load, cantilever moment, simply supported cases; shim regression. |
+| `Beam3D` | Supported | Closed-form biaxial bending, torsion, grillage; 183-value frozen low-level/frame oracle; 309-value progression/transient oracle; 3D portal shim regression. |
+
+### Solver/system and I/O
+
+| Capability | Status | Evidence / limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `StructSystem` unique ownership and destruction order | Supported | `test_structsystem`; sanitizer suite; frame/shim tests. Elements observe dependencies; same-system membership is not yet enforced. |
+| Constraints and explicit stepping | Supported for tested frame workflows | Direct system tests plus frame/shim regressions. |
+| Element kill/free-particle ownership transfer | Existing behavior, further hardening pending | Ownership containers preserve lifetime; #44 owns checked removal/membership rules. |
+| CSV/model filesystem writers on `StructSystem` | Supported legacy behavior, architecturally coupled | R1 preserves output schemas. #46 isolates I/O without changing schemas. |
+| `isFileExists`, `isDirExists`, `makedir` | Internal | Tested as filesystem helpers but not retained as installed public API. |
+| `Config` | Internal legacy / unsafe to export as-is | Header-defined ordinary functions create ODR risk; no production caller evidence. |
+
+## Existing validation evidence on the modern baseline
+
+The R1 modernization issue records these mandatory evidence families for the
+current code state:
+
+- native Beam2D/Beam3D and shim fixtures, including the heavy 3D portal case;
+- frozen C++/Fortran parity: 183 low-level/stage values;
+- frozen progression/transient parity: 309 values;
+- ASan + UBSan native validation;
+- focused unit suites for element construction, grid section, integrator,
+  material, particle, section, and `StructSystem`.
+
+A supported status above identifies which of those checks directly establishes a
+particular family. Passing frame parity does not prove untested material, section,
+or continuum formulations.
+
+## Separate continuum feature branch inventory
+
+`feature/solid-tet-fracture@b83e9211cc7b3fa62712a1c3f9c2058cff583eea`
+contains substantial implementation work that is **not** part of the modern
+production baseline.
+
+| Feature-branch item | R1 status | Evidence present there | Why it is not promoted by #40 |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `ShellTri3` | Experimental, external branch only | `tests/test_shell.cpp`: rigid motion, membrane patch, cantilever bending, membrane plasticity, shim erosion/damage; final test harness reports accumulated checks/failures. | Branch predates the modern ownership/API baseline; constructor passes no beam section; formulation-specific validation has not been reconciled with current contracts or frozen-oracle policy. |
+| `SolidTet4` | Experimental, external branch only | `tests/test_solidtet.cpp`: SVK statics/equilibrium, rigid motion, brittle failure/damage, J2 plasticity sanity, shim erosion/damage, ground contact. | Same integration gap; no current modern-branch public contract or accepted continuum oracle. |
+| continuum WASM additions | Experimental, external branch only | Shim contains `vf_add_tet`, `vf_add_shell`, failure/damage tracking and contact paths. | #48 only migrates accepted binding capabilities; #51 defines concrete continuum follow-up evidence. |
+
+The feature branch demonstrates two architecture requirements that R1 must
+support even before integrating those formulations:
+
+1. shell/solid constructors intentionally use no beam `BaseSection`;
+2. local node order is geometric data and must not be inferred from the
+   ID-sorted `BaseElement::particles_` map.
+
+Do **not** wholesale copy the feature branch's older raw-pointer implementation
+into the modern branch. Port/reconcile formulation code only after #43/#45
+contracts and #51 verification requirements are in place.
+
+## Explicit unresolved numerical limitations
+
+These limitations must remain visible in documentation and failure behavior:
+
+- `UniPower` constitutive history/correctness TODO is unresolved.
+- calculated shear center (`SHy`, `SHz`) is not implemented for `Ctube`,
+  `AngleSteel`, or `Rectangle`; returning stored zero must not be represented as a
+  verified physical value.
+- translation mass-matrix integration is not implemented and is deliberately
+  rejected by `Particle::solve*`.
+- `PlaneElement` and `SolidElement` are not usable formulations on the modern
+  baseline.
+- no frame regression can validate ShellTri3/SolidTet4 continuum correctness.
+- no universal result API, parallel assembly contract, GPU path, full shell/solid
+  port, or general continuum constitutive framework is an R1 requirement.
