+# R1 public API migration map
+
+**Source baseline:** `refactor/modern-cpp@32800f03a5d47f997b1a0c70460bad83fcf7faf7`
+
+This map is the implementation contract for the first layout/namespace move in
+#42. #40 does not move these files; it records exactly where current declarations
+belong so #41/#42 can execute without redesigning the API during mechanical edits.
+
+## Migration rules
+
+1. Public types move into the single namespace `openvfife`.
+2. Existing class/type names stay unchanged during the move.
+3. Public include paths change from repository-relative `headers/*.h` to
+   `<openvfife/.../*.hpp>`.
+4. No global compatibility aliases are created by default.
+5. Internal helpers are not installed merely because they historically lived in
+   `headers/`.
+6. Experimental headers are explicitly includable but are omitted from the
+   initial supported umbrella header.
+7. Unimplemented element scaffolding is not advertised as usable capability.
+8. Numerical formulas, iteration order, frozen fixtures, reference data and
+   tolerances are not changed by the layout migration.
+
+## Header and source destination map
+
+| Current header | Current source | Destination public header | Destination implementation | Public status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `headers/particle.h` | `src/particle.cpp` | `include/openvfife/core/particle.hpp` | `src/core/particle.cpp` | Supported public |
+| `headers/material.h` | `src/material.cpp` | `include/openvfife/material/material.hpp` | `src/material/material.cpp` | Mixed supported/experimental public; capability table governs |
+| `headers/section.h` | `src/section.cpp` | `include/openvfife/section/section.hpp` | `src/section/section.cpp` | Mixed supported/experimental public; capability table governs |
+| `headers/integrator.h` | `src/integrator.cpp` | `include/openvfife/numerics/quadrature.hpp` | `src/numerics/quadrature.cpp` | Supported public |
+| `headers/gridsection.h` | `src/gridsection.cpp` | `include/openvfife/section/grid_section.hpp` | `src/section/grid_section.cpp` | Experimental public; direct include only initially |
+| `headers/element.h` | `src/element.cpp` | `include/openvfife/element/element.hpp` | `src/element/element.cpp` | Mixed supported/experimental/unimplemented; capability table governs |
+| `headers/structsystem.h` | `src/structsystem.cpp` | `include/openvfife/solver/struct_system.hpp` | `src/solver/struct_system.cpp` | `StructSystem` supported public; filesystem helpers become internal |
+| `headers/config.hpp` | header-only ordinary definitions | **No installed public header in R1 as-is** | `src/io/config.hpp` plus `.cpp` if retained by #46 | Internal legacy |
+| n/a | `wasm/vfife_shim.cpp` | n/a | `bindings/wasm/vfife_shim.cpp` | Binding/internal C++ implementation; exported C ABI handled by #48 |
+
+The mapping intentionally keeps coherent historical declarations together for the
+first move. R1 does not mechanically split every class into a separate file.
+Further splits are justified only by dependency or consumer needs.
+
