+### `headers/config.hpp`
+
+`Config` is **not** included in the installed public API during R1. The current
+header defines ordinary non-inline functions and stream operators, so including it
+from multiple translation units risks ODR/multiple-definition failures. #46 owns
+splitting definitions into implementation code or removing/replacing the legacy
+utility if it remains unused.
+
+## Include migration examples
+
+### Before
+
+```cpp
+#include "../../headers/structsystem.h"
+#include "../../headers/material.h"
+
+StructSystem system(1);
+LinearElastic steel(1);
+```
+
+### After #42
+
+```cpp
+#include <openvfife/material/material.hpp>
+#include <openvfife/solver/struct_system.hpp>
+
+openvfife::StructSystem system(1);
+openvfife::LinearElastic steel(1);
+```
+
+or, for a consumer that intentionally accepts the supported umbrella surface:
+
+```cpp
+#include <openvfife/openvfife.hpp>
+
+openvfife::StructSystem system(1);
+```
+
+## Repository callers that must migrate
+
+#42/#48/#50 must update all repository-owned callers rather than relying on
+compatibility aliases:
+
+- `src/*.cpp` relative header includes;
+- `tests/*.cpp`, including frozen-oracle probes;
+- `wasm/vfife_shim.cpp` when it moves to `bindings/wasm/`;
+- native and sanitizer build scripts until #41 replaces source-list ownership
+  with canonical CMake targets;
+- examples and user/developer documentation;
+- any browser/WASM build script that names old source paths.
+
+Generated WASM artifacts are not evidence of successful migration. #48 must build
+fresh artifacts from the new canonical library target and exercise the worker
+contract.
+
+## Source/ABI compatibility
+
+The historical public line is 1.x (`README.md` refers to version 1.0 and
+`WIKI.md` records v1.02). Changing both include prefixes and the C++ namespace is
+a deliberate source break. R1 therefore:
+
+- does not promise source compatibility with the historical global namespace;
+- does not promise binary ABI compatibility;
+- should use a new major public compatibility line if released (for example a
+  2.x line, with pre-releases while the migration is being integrated);
+- gives experimental declarations no stability guarantee;
+- keeps current class names during the move to make mechanical migration obvious
+  and reviewable.
+
+## Acceptance checks for the eventual move
+
+The migration is not complete merely because repository sources compile. Later
+issues must prove, at one exact SHA:
+
+1. each installed public header compiles independently;
+2. a relocated external two-translation-unit consumer uses only the installed
+   package and `openVFIFE::openvfife`;
+3. the install remains usable after moving the prefix;
+4. Eigen headers remain available to downstream public signatures offline;
+5. native fixtures, 183-value and 309-value frozen parity, and ASan/UBSan stay
+   green;
+6. WASM is freshly rebuilt from the canonical target and worker smoke checks pass;
+7. documented examples compile against the new public include prefix.
